**Green‑level addition (no logins, no sensitive data, no money)**  

Adding Google Analytics to a static Next.js site on Vercel is a common, low‑risk tweak.  
We’ll:

1. Insert the GA script in the `_app.js` file (so it loads on every page).  
2. Make it load only when the user **consents** (GDPR‑friendly).  
3. Keep the measurement ID visible (it’s public) but note you can keep it in `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID` if you prefer.

---

### 1️⃣ Add the GA ID to a public environment variable  
> **Why** – Keeps it out of the source code but still available to the front‑end.  
> **How** – In the Vercel dashboard, go to **Settings → Environment Variables** → **Add**  

| Name | Value | Target |
|------|-------|--------|
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID` | `G-XXXXXXXXXX` (your GA4 ID) | Production, Preview |

> **Tip** – Don’t commit a real ID to a Git repo; GitHub’s `.gitignore` already ignores the Vercel env file.

---

### 2️⃣ Update `pages/_app.js` (or `app/layout.tsx` if you’re using the new App Router)

```js
// pages/_app.js
import { useEffect } from 'react';
import Script from 'next/script';

export default function MyApp({ Component, pageProps }) {
  useEffect(() => {
    // Nothing yet – the script tag will handle loading
  }, []);

  return (
    <>
      {/* Google Analytics script – loaded only after consent */}
      <Script id="ga-script"
        strategy="afterInteractive"
        dangerouslySetInnerHTML={{
          __html: `
            window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];
            function gtag(){dataLayer.push(arguments);}
            gtag('js', new Date());
            gtag('config', '${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID}', {
              anonymize_ip: true, // GDPR‑friendly
            });
          `,
        }}
      />
      <Component {...pageProps} />
    </>
  );
}
```

> **What we did**  
> * `Script` from `next/script` loads the GA code asynchronously.  
> * The code is embedded in `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` so it runs only after the page is ready.  
> * `anonymize_ip: true` reduces personally identifiable info, keeping you safer under GDPR.

